From cde5a08f0eda9dfd869f7ba088898565f93657d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: derive timeout from exact frame
 duration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HSTX and LPRX timeouts must cover at least one complete frame.  The
existing calculation uses drm_mode_vrefresh(), which rounds to the
nearest integer before the duration is calculated.  A mode just below
an integer refresh rate therefore gets a timeout shorter than its real
frame duration.

The PineTab-V panel exposes the problem: its 66 MHz, 854 by 1295 timing
is 59.678 Hz, but it is rounded to 60 Hz for the timeout.

Calculate the frame duration directly from the pixel clock and totals,
and round up to a TX byte clock.  This preserves the minimum-frame
requirement without a board-specific refresh-rate margin.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
index 9bfd1a658..bec79095d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
@@ -900,10 +900,13 @@ static void cdns_dsi_bridge_atomic_pre_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	/*
 	 * HSTX and LPRX timeouts are both expressed in TX byte clk cycles and
 	 * both should be set to at least the time it takes to transmit a
-	 * frame.
+	 * frame.  drm_mode_vrefresh() rounds to the nearest integer, which can
+	 * make the timeout shorter than one frame for modes just below an
+	 * integer refresh rate.  Derive the duration from the exact timings.
 	 */
-	tmp = NSEC_PER_SEC / drm_mode_vrefresh(mode);
-	tmp /= tx_byte_period;
+	tmp = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL((u64)mode->crtc_htotal * mode->crtc_vtotal *
+			       NSEC_PER_SEC,
+			       (u64)mode->crtc_clock * 1000 * tx_byte_period);
 
 	for (div = 0; div <= CLK_DIV_MAX; div++) {
 		if (tmp <= HSTX_TIMEOUT_MAX)
